From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: "Features…" in the app menu opens the control centre in the VM

What: while OmacVM.app runs the VM, the app menu (the one named after the VM's
app) has "Features…" under "About". A click posts a distributed notification
under the name the launcher put in OMACVM_FEATURES_REQUEST (its bundle id and
process id); the launcher (ControlCentreRoute.swift) runs the VM's
src/control/guest/open.sh through the guest agent, which opens OmacVM's
control centre on the VM's desktop (one window, in front), and says in an
alert what is missing when it cannot (nobody logged in, control centre off,
an older OmacVM in the VM). Without OMACVM_FEATURES_REQUEST (QEMU not started
by OmacVM.app) the menu is unchanged.
Why: the launcher's own menu is not shown while the VM runs (QEMU's window is
in front), and the control centre had no route from the Mac's side
(design: one UI, in the VM; user 2026-10-05 00:15).
Safety: QEMU sends nothing but the click: no data, no reply read. Any process
of the same user could post the same name; all it does is open the control
centre in the VM.
Upstream: not applicable (OmacVM's launcher).
Test: build time, the patched ui/cocoa.m must call omacvm_add_features_item
(build-qemu-gpu-runtime.sh); the guest side in src/tests/cc-open.sh; the menu
itself in the test app on the Mac mini (tracks: cc-routes).

diff --git a/ui/cocoa.m b/ui/cocoa.m
--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -2795,6 +2795,49 @@
     [menu setDelegate:omacvm_memory_menu];
 }
 
+/*
+ * OmacVM: "Features…" in the app menu (omacvm-cocoa-features-menu.patch)
+ * opens OmacVM's control centre on the VM's desktop. QEMU only passes the
+ * click on: a distributed notification under the name OmacVM.app gave
+ * (OMACVM_FEATURES_REQUEST, its own bundle id and process id); the app runs
+ * the VM's script for it through the guest agent and says what is missing.
+ */
+@interface OmacvmFeaturesItem : NSObject
+- (void)open:(id)sender;
+@end
+
+static OmacvmFeaturesItem *omacvm_features_item;
+
+@implementation OmacvmFeaturesItem
+- (void)open:(id)sender
+{
+    const char *name = getenv("OMACVM_FEATURES_REQUEST");
+    if (!name || !*name) {
+        return;
+    }
+    [[NSDistributedNotificationCenter defaultCenter]
+        postNotificationName:[NSString stringWithUTF8String:name]
+                      object:nil
+                    userInfo:nil
+          deliverImmediately:YES];
+}
+@end
+
+static void omacvm_add_features_item(NSMenu *menu)
+{
+    const char *name = getenv("OMACVM_FEATURES_REQUEST");
+    if (!name || !*name) {
+        return; /* not started by OmacVM.app: nobody to ask */
+    }
+    omacvm_features_item = [[OmacvmFeaturesItem alloc] init];
+    NSMenuItem *item = [[[NSMenuItem alloc] initWithTitle:@"Features…"
+                                                   action:@selector(open:)
+                                            keyEquivalent:@""] autorelease];
+    [item setTarget:omacvm_features_item];
+    [item setToolTip:@"OmacVM's control centre in the VM: features on or off, repair, updates"];
+    [menu addItem:item];
+}
+
 static void create_initial_menus(void)
 {
     // Add menus
@@ -2807,6 +2850,7 @@ static void create_initial_menus(void)
     // Application menu
     menu = [[NSMenu alloc] initWithTitle:@""];
     [menu addItemWithTitle:[NSString stringWithFormat:@"About %@", omacvm_product_name()] action:@selector(do_about_menu_item:) keyEquivalent:@""];
+    omacvm_add_features_item(menu);
     omacvm_add_memory_items(menu);
     [menu addItem:[NSMenuItem separatorItem]]; //Separator
     menuItem = [menu addItemWithTitle:@"Services" action:nil keyEquivalent:@""];
